\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S2.2}{\ignorespaces Plasmode, H2a condition (features swapped within era): per-fold AUC (percent) by $\gamma $ for pipelines with adjustment, and the R1 decision at $\gamma =1$. Under H2a a legitimate era effect remains in the features and the AUC has no universal chance level, so this is a conditional stress test and the R1 decisions are descriptive. The paired difference of raw adjustment against no adjustment at $\gamma =1$ was +9.4 pp (95\% CI +6.9 to +11.9) for the random forest (30 replicates) and +8.6 pp (+6.0 to +11.3) for XGBoost (20); at $\gamma =0$ it was +0.1 ($-$2.6 to +2.8) and +1.3 pp ($-$1.3 to +3.9); descriptive, from the stored replicates (addendum 3, S2.11).\relax }}{13}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
